        <detaileddescription>
<para>Parses the next command line argument if there is a match in longval or shortval. <parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>arg</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>CommandlineArg to fill in with details about argument that was parsed. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>max_values</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The maximum number of values of parse if they exist. The number of values in arg will be &lt;= this value. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>longval</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The long argument name such as &quot;--help&quot; </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>shortval</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The short argument character. &apos;h&apos; for example would mean check for &quot;-h&quot; </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>true if the argument was parsed. If returning true, the <ref refid="class_cmdline_parser" kindref="compound">CmdlineParser</ref> advances to the next argument. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
